values ('f1ecfbd9-19e3-5ca1-a70c-6c6c4b135d68', 'rg3-word-parts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Plot Number Nine$q$, $q$Every Saturday, Amara walks to the community garden on Pine Street. The garden has twenty small plots, and each family takes care of one. Amara's family has plot number nine.

This spring, plot nine looked sad. A storm had knocked down the bean poles, and half the rows were still unplanted. Amara felt hopeless at first. There was so much work to do!

Mr. Okafor, who has the plot next door, came over to help. "Let's replant the beans along the fence," he said. "They will be safer there." Mr. Okafor was very helpful. He showed Amara how to tie the new poles so they would not wobble.

Then Amara made a mistake. While pulling weeds, Amara pulled up a tiny pepper plant too. "I was careless," Amara said. Mr. Okafor smiled. "That is fixable. We can put it back in the soil gently."

By June, plot nine was full of green leaves. Amara picked the first beans and shared them with Mr. Okafor. Being a good gardener takes patience, Amara thought, and so does being a good neighbor.$q$, 'draft')
