   $q$The referee said "the field was playable." Using the suffix -able, what does "playable" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"able to be played on","is_correct":true},{"text":"already played on","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-tense"},{"text":"a person who plays","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-able-with-er"},{"text":"too wet to play on","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$able to be played on$q$, $q$The suffix -able means "can be," so "playable" means able to be played on, and the players then "ran out" to start the game. If the field were too wet to play on, the game would have been canceled.$q$, 'draft', '6b295ff7-237c-5b5e-aacc-7ca2c2cbbb3d')
